{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>And I asked her, and I placed, etc.</b> He altered his account out of suspicion of their cunning, for they might say that he gave the objects before inquiring after her family, and these matters concern her father. Therefore he preempted by stating that he gave nothing until after he knew that she was the daughter of Betuel, fit for Isaac; he gave them to her with the status of a bride's adornments from the groom, and her father has no claim upon them."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:10.256449098Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}